## 1. frontend-slides — Zara Zhang

- Source: https://github.com/zarazhangrui/frontend-slides
- License: MIT
- Copyright (c) 2025 Zara Zhang

**What is derived from it, and where it lives here:**

| This repo | Origin | Modified? |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `reference/STYLE_PRESETS.md` | `STYLE_PRESETS.md` | unchanged |
| `reference/viewport-base.css` | `viewport-base.css` | unchanged |
| `reference/html-template.md` | `html-template.md` | unchanged |
| `reference/animation-patterns.md` | `animation-patterns.md` | unchanged |
| `scripts/extract-pptx.py` | `scripts/extract-pptx.py` | unchanged |
| `SKILL.md` | `SKILL.md` | **substantially rewritten** — see below |

`SKILL.md` is a new document. It reuses the upstream skill's core concepts
(fixed-stage layout model, progressive template disclosure, show-don't-tell
style discovery, anti-AI-slop design guidance) and restructures them around a
portrait-first default canvas, a bundled visual style gallery, cross-agent
(Claude Code / Codex) portability, expanded CJK typography rules, and
always-on inline editing.

